  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pension Public  Awareness and Literacy IDF Grant Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot; The main objective of this project is to strengthen capacity of the Ministry of Labor and Social Issues and its State Social Security Service to ensure financial literacy and awareness component of the Pension Reform. The Project will help develop and introduce permanent tools for improving  financial literacy and continuously raising awareness on pensions, and pilot specific targeted campaigns which will help increase efficiency of further interventions. Also, it is aimed at increasing awareness and public education on integrated social services centers, as well as specific components of the Social Protection Administration Project of the World Bank (loan No. 7848AM). Taking into consideration the importance of the financial literacy and awareness component of the pension reform, and the fact that it is a cross cutting initiative related not only to the social sector, the Ministry of Labor and Social Issues initiated establishment of a specialized institution- Pension System Awareness Center Foundation (PSACF or the Foundation). The establishment decree has been passed by the Government in July 2011. The board of trustees of the Foundation is chaired by the Head of the State Social Security Service and the Deputy Minister of Labor and Social Issues. The Ministry of Labor and Social Issues is the main responsible institution for the pension reform and the Foundation is in a position to help the Ministry and the other institutions involved to ensure the effective implementation of the financial literacy component of the reform. The Foundation has its high quality professional staff, procedures and policies in place and is managing projects funded by the Armenian and US Governments. It will also be involved in managing this Project in cooperation with the Foreign Financing Projects Management Center of the Ministry of Finance. The overall outcomes of this project are: &quot;&quot;   Strengthened capacity of MLSI to deliver awareness, financial knowledge and high quality services &quot;&quot;   Strengthened capacity to ensure public support and trust to the pension, as well as social services reforms &quot;&quot;   Successful operation of pension funds, which will lead to investments, new jobs, and poverty reduction TF013654&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
